  "summary": "Three preprints pair spatial domain and scRNA-seq cluster calls with formal significance tests, while PRISM and stochprofIC model contamination and noise.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is replacing heuristic outputs in single-cell and spatial transcriptomics with explicitly modelled error. SigDoTS applies hypothesis testing with FWER control to spatial domains, merging or retaining candidates via null simulations. ProClust tests scRNA-seq cluster significance, merging overclustered groups using log-concave cluster modelling and projection-based testing. A related generative-model strand appears in PRISM, an EM framework jointly modelling ambient RNA, doublets and cell-type assignment, and in stochprofIC, which uses distributional regression to correct noise and batch effects when inferring state variability. Organotchi and SubCellSeg are imaging segmentation tools and sit outside this statistical thread. The new element is pairing each partition or correction with an explicit null or noise model.",
